==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Brainwashed Whale Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Brainwashed Island Cat''' after obtaining from [[Adrift in Fear (Merciless)]] and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
Brainwashed Fish Cat is a copy of [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Fish Cat]] with Strong vs Zombies and Zombie Killer instead of Strong vs [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] and [[Critical Hit]] as well as a negligible boost to its health and damage. Because it relies on weak but fast-paced attacks, it's unlikely to deliver a huge amount of damage before a zombie burrows. As such, its utility ultimately stems from cleaning up burrowed zombies to reconnect cat units across the battlefield. Since Zombies typically don't burrow in huge groups, its single target doesn't hinder it too much, and its short attack animation allows it to immediately take away a portion of zombies' health while they're still unburrowing.

=== '''True Form''' ===
True Form gains Toxic Immunity and a 50% chance to Curse Zombies. Although Zombies rely mostly on stats, many common ones have annoying abilities, such as [[Zir Zeal]]'s Freeze. [[Death Angel Z-Onel|Z-Onel]], [[Daboo of the Dead|Daboo]] and [[Big Peng Z]] are also reliant on debuffs, making this unit a potentially valuable asset against them. Toxic Immunity isn't a game changer, but it does expand this unit's use. On top of countering Big Peng Z, [[Zollow]], and [[Oldstrich]], it can also be a serviceable Toxic Immune attacker if the need arises in certain stages.

